{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773873120,"nonce":"csKNmeR5QyUq5i9/ErLWnNPSBjA=","message":"Additional scope: API key must be the de jure official path for public release.\n\nThe SDK backend should support two authentication modes:\n1. API key (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY env var) — official, documented, what public users will use\n2. OAuth credential reuse from ~/.claude/credentials — works locally for the repo owner, but undocumented and not surfaced in any public-facing code or docs\n\nThe SDK likely already supports both (it reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY if set, falls back to OAuth token). The work here is:\n- Verify this behavior in @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk\n- Ensure the API key path is the one documented in any README/setup guide\n- Ensure no code comments describe the OAuth credential source or how to obtain/locate those tokens\n- The OAuth path can remain functional locally (for the repo owner) as long as it is not documented anywhere in the public history\n\nThis means the public app is fully usable with a legitimate API key, and the OAuth convenience is a local-only undocumented implementation detail.","files":null}]}